From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Silva <nical@fastmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jan 2025 16:13:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] [moz] Remove -fno-exceptions in AddLLVM.cmake.

There has to be a better way to this, I have not found it yet.

DXC uses exceptions. If -fno-exceptions is passed during the build, clang-cl produces
a fair amount of errors caused by the presence of try and throw statements in various
places such as:
 - lib/Support/ErrorHandling.cpp
 - include/llvm/ADT/ilist.h
 - lib/Support/FoldingSet.cpp

For part of the build, exceptions can be enabled by passing -DLLVM_REQUIRES_EH to the
cmake invocation. Unfortunately, the build has a multi-step process which involves
compiling DXC (and LLVM) for the host (in addition to the target OS) to generate some
tables which are fed into the build for the target configuration.
That extra build step runs cmake a second time during the build and I have not found
how to get that invocation to enable exceptions, leading to the compilation errors.

As a workaround, this commit comments out the line that passes -fnoexceptions in
AddLLVM.make. AddLLVM.cmake comes from the upstream llvm repository.
A better solution would probably set LLVM_REQUIRES_EH from whichever piece of the
build is causing the LLVM inclusion for the host build step.

I am also somewhat nervous about having exceptions enabled in a DLL that is called
by Firfox which does not enable exceptions. From a quick test it looks like unwinding
stops at the C function boundary and std::terminate is called, but I haven't found
some definitive wording about this behavior.

Note that Dawn also explicitly enables exceptions in their DXC build and I expect
that Chrome, much like Firefox, disables C++ exceptions.
---
 cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake b/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake
index 9b92e3f22..424c8a532 100644
--- a/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake
+++ b/cmake/modules/AddLLVM.cmake
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ function(llvm_update_compile_flags name)
     endif()
   else()
     if(LLVM_COMPILER_IS_GCC_COMPATIBLE)
-      list(APPEND LLVM_COMPILE_FLAGS "-fno-exceptions")
+      #list(APPEND LLVM_COMPILE_FLAGS "-fno-exceptions")
     elseif(MSVC)
       list(APPEND LLVM_COMPILE_DEFINITIONS _HAS_EXCEPTIONS=0)
       list(APPEND LLVM_COMPILE_FLAGS "/EHs-c-")
